class Solution {
    public int digitFrequencyScore(int n) {
        // Array to store frequency of digits 0–9
        int[] freq = new int[10];   
        while (n > 0) {
            int digit = n % 10;     // Get the last digit
            freq[digit]++;         // Increment frequency for that digit
            n /= 10;               // Remove the last digit
        }
        int score = 0;
        // Calculate score: digit * frequency for each digit
        for (int d = 0; d < 10; d++) {
            score += d * freq[d];
        }
        return score;
    }
}

Time Complexity: 
𝑂(log⁡10(𝑛)) ≈ proportional to the number of digits.

Space Complexity: 
𝑂(1).
